sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Controller
  participant L as Workload group
  participant W as Inspection worker
  participant D as Resource teardown
  C->>L: TERM, group deadline scope
  Note over C,L: T = TERM start + grace, at most 2 seconds
  L-->>C: Leader exit notification (no reap)
  Note over C,W: No inspection during group grace, even after leader exit
  C->>L: At T: unconditional group KILL attempt
  Note over C,W: Advance epoch, including a denied attempt
  Note over C,L: K = T + A, A at most 2 seconds
  C->>W: One final query after KILL and observed exit, deadline K minus R
  Note over W: Example failure: helper creation or wait stalls
  C->>W: At cutoff: retire worker, bounded cleanup starts
  C->>C: At K minus R: close target signal authority
  C->>L: Nonblocking leader reap attempts, only through K
  C->>D: Continue cleanup and disposal
  W-->>C: Late result (if any)
  C->>C: Retain as rejected, never change failed verdict
  Note over C,D: One scheduler serves teardown and worker timers, no extra target allowance
